ShaQ - On-Demand Local Errand & Verification
ServiceShaQ is a service that provides real people to solve small, everyday problems for people in Pakistan. It is designed to clear people's doubts (Shaq) and save time for busy individuals who cannot leave their work or home.   Currently, I am a 1st-semester BS Computer Systems Engineering student building this startup idea from scratch.
🚨 The Problem We Solve
Doubt & Anxiety:People often leave home and worry if they locked the door, left the iron on, or forgot their keys.   Lack of Time: Busy professionals do not have time for simple tasks like taking a bike to the mechanic, or picking up small items.   
💡 The Solution & Services
Customers can request a trusted, local worker to go to a specific location immediately to act as their eyes and hands.   Verification (The "Shaq" Feature): Checking locked doors, verifying if a shop is open, or finding forgotten items.   Live Updates: Visiting a repair shop to see the real progress of a device when the shop owner isn't answering.   Small Errands & Drop-offs: Dropping off a bike for tuning, delivering documents, or everyday shopping.   
💼 Business Model & Impact
Zero Investment for Workers: Unlike ride-hailing apps, ShaQ workers can operate on foot or bicycle for nearby neighborhood tasks, providing instant jobs for unemployed youth.   Affordable: Customers pay a small, reasonable fee (e.g., 200 to 300 Rs) for quick tasks, saving them fuel and time.   
